Executive Education

	Philosophy

		-
			Executive education is education where the focus is redirected from being able to
			complete advanced tasks manually and unaided, to having enough of a high-level
			understanding of a subject that the execution of advanced tasks within it may be
			effectively delegated to third parties.
		-

	Principles

		Context

			-
				Executive education becomes more relevant as society becomes more dependent on AI
				systems.
				
				As such, the workings of AI models themselves become a topic of importance.
			-

		Methods

			-
				A core method for executive education is to inspect, critique, and edit the results
				of delegated work.
			-